      "Long ago, by the sparkling blue Sea of Galilee, there lived a fisherman named Simon. He was tall and strong, with rough hands and a loud, kind laugh. He worked on the boats with his brother Andrew, and he loved the sea almost as much as he loved his family.",
      "Simon was not a perfect man. He had a quick tongue and a quicker temper, and he said things before he thought about them. But his heart was honest and his courage was big — and Andrew knew that special things were about to happen.",
      "One day, Andrew rushed to Simon with wonderful news. 'We have found someone!' he said. 'His name is Jesus.' He took Simon to meet him. Jesus looked at the big fisherman kindly and said: 'You will be called Peter, which means Rock.' Simon had no idea what that meant — but somehow, he knew he was safe.",
      "Jesus called the brothers to follow him: 'Come with me, and I will make you fishers of people.' Without a moment's hesitation, Peter left his nets and his boat and followed Jesus. From that day on, he never once turned back.",
      "One stormy night, Jesus walked right across the wild waves toward the boat. 'If it is really you,' Peter called, 'tell me to come to you!' So Jesus said, 'Come!' And Peter climbed out of the boat — and walked on the water too! But when he felt the wind, he grew afraid and began to sink. Jesus caught his hand at once. 'Why did you doubt?' he smiled. Even when he wobbled, Peter was the bravest one in the boat.",
      "One day, Jesus asked his friends a question: 'Who do you say I am?' Peter answered without stopping to think: 'You are the Christ, the Son of the living God!' Jesus was so happy. 'You are Peter,' he said, 'and on this rock I will build my Church. I give you the keys of the kingdom of heaven.'",
      "But there came a dark, sad night. Peter had promised Jesus he would never leave him. Yet when Jesus was arrested, Peter was frightened, and three times he said he did not even know Jesus. Then a rooster crowed — just as Jesus had said it would. Peter ran away and wept and wept, so ashamed of his shaky courage.",
      "After Jesus rose from the dead, he came to find Peter by the sea. 'Peter, do you love me?' Jesus asked. 'Yes, Lord,' Peter said. 'Feed my sheep,' Jesus said. Again he asked — and again. All three times Peter said 'Yes, you know I love you,' and all three times Jesus answered gently: 'Feed my sheep.' Jesus forgave him completely, and gave him the biggest job of all: to take care of everyone in the Church.",
      "Peter was never frightened again. At Pentecost, the once-shaky fisherman stood in front of a huge crowd and spoke bravely about Jesus — and on that one day, thousands of people were baptized. Peter healed the sick, prayed over the broken, and even raised his friend Tabitha from the dead. Everywhere he went, people felt the love of Jesus.",
      "In the end, Peter travelled to the great city of Rome, and there he led and loved the whole Church — the very first Pope, holding the keys Jesus had given him. When he was captured, he asked to be crucified upside down, because he said he was not worthy to die exactly as Jesus did. Today, every Pope carries on Peter's work, and his grave rests under St Peter's Basilica in Rome — the rock on which the Church still stands.",
