      "After two weeks, Maximilian was the last one alive. On August 14, the eve of Our Lady's great feast, he held out his arm peacefully — wearing, at last, the red crown he had chosen as a boy.",
      "In 1982, Maximilian Kolbe was declared a saint — a “martyr of charity.” The man whose life he saved was there to see it! St Maximilian shows us what love really means: laying down your life for a friend, the way Jesus did.",
